WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:19.666
TK: I'm Tom Kornberg. I'm on the faculty at UCSF in the Cardiovascular Research Institute,

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:26.399
where I actually work on fruit flies. EA: ...Drosophila, just in case you didn't know what it was called.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:33.199
And I'm Emanuel Ax, who has nothing to do with flies, or fruit for that matter,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:40.899
but we do make music together and we're old classmates.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:47.166
I was I guess mainly a music major and you were a music and science major.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:55.699
TK: To be fair we were classmates at Columbia College. We were also classmates at the Juilliard School,

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.366
which was at that time right across the street. So that does date us.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:03.666
EA: That's true, that's true. ...Well, the building is still there.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:08.966
TK: But I would say that I was a Columbia student, who took performance classes:

00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:14.566
Orchestra, Chamber Music and lessons at Juilliard. You really were a Juilliard student...

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:20.532
EA: ... who took classes at Columbia, including a biochemistry course. Which was very exciting.

00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:23.899
TK: You used some textbook, which you....

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.732
EA: I used the Watson textbook "The Molecular Biology of the Gene,"

00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:33.132
which I still think is the best textbook I've ever seen about anything.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:37.632
Because I picked up the book and I actually understood something.

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:40.666
And I think with that subject it's a miracle.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:47.599
I must say I'm totally dazzled by the fact that you've kept up your playing so wonderfully.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:55.132
And I wish I could come do research with you the way you play with me.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:02:01.099
TK: So over the years since we were students, your travels, your tours

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.366
have frequently brought you to San Francisco.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:06.366
And on the occasions where the time has permitted

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:10.166
we've enjoyed getting together to play chamber music. EA: Right.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:15.999
TK: And so this is a special pleasure after all these years to be doing something really serious...

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.866
EA: Well, the pleasure is all mine.

00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:26.399
And I guess we're going to do the first movement of the Beethoven cello Sonata in A major, opus 69.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:34.132
TK: Allegro ma non troppo. EA: If you say so!

00:02:34.133 --> 00:16:13.600
Sonata...

